[AGENT] It sounds like the stress is creating a real barrier, making it impossible to find time for your meals and leading you to skip food. Feeling like you just don't have the time for your meals when you are under stress is a very real and painful experience. This is a common way our bodies react when we are overwhelmed, and it doesn't reflect a lack of desire to eat. You might try to schedule very small, non-negotiable eating windows, perhaps just focusing on one small snack or a glass of water at a specific time each day. You could also look into simple meal preparation strategies, like having pre-cut vegetables or quick protein options ready to go, so that when time is tight, you can still manage to fuel yourself. Remember that even tiny amounts of consistent nourishment can help manage that stress response.

